    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_9",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Phyllocnistis liquidambarisella is a moth of the Gracillariidae family, known from the United States (New York, Maryland, Kentucky, Georgia, Texas, Florida). The hostplant for the species is \"Liquidambar styraciflua\". They mine the leaves of their host plant. The mine has the form of a long, winding, linear mine on the upperside of the leaf. It is rather indistinct, without any central line of frass.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.999999995794773,
